   "text": "Reading the drawing:\n\n- The central carbon has three drawn bonds and an implicit hydrogen. It bears CO2H on a wedge pointing up, an OTBDPS group at the lower left, and a methyl group at the lower right.\n- TBDPS is the tert-butyldiphenylsilyl group, Si(Ph)2C(CH3)3, so the oxygen is O\u2013Si(C6H5)2C(CH3)3.\n- This is therefore lactic acid with its hydroxyl protected as the TBDPS ether.\n\nFor the stereochemistry, the CO2H is on a wedge toward the viewer, so the implicit hydrogen points away. The CIP priorities are O > CO2H > CH3 > H. Going from O (lower left) to CO2H (up) to CH3 (lower right) is clockwise with H at the back, so the centre is R.\n\nIn SMILES, writing the neighbours in the order CH3, H, O, CO2H, `@@` corresponds to R.\n\nSMILES: C[C@@H](O[Si](c1ccccc1)(c1ccccc1)C(C)(C)C)C(=O)O"
